## Prototyping Infrastructure

The operational circuit is arranged and structured using standard embedded design tools:
- Breadboard: Functions as the physical mounting grid to share common power tracks and hold component leads side-by-side.
- Jumper Wires: Serve as the point-to-point connections making up the signal, power, and ground networks of the local architecture.
